Multiple Sequence Alignment using Multi Group Genetic Algorithm

1. Intro
  This program solves multiple sequence alignmenat problem as 
  combinatorial problem. 
  This program executes Multi Group Genetic Algorithm on 
  Paralell Machine PIM model-m, or Distributed KLIC system 
  installed on multi-processor machine.
  As the resulte, we can get better quality alignment quickly.
  This system can get better solution than best-first search and converge
  faster than multi hill-climbing.
  And sometimes crossover operation is effective for improvemnet of
  solutions.

2. Abstract
   We have succeeded in solving protein sequence analysis problems by
   applying an original multi-group parallel genetic algorithm. It has 
   been shown recently that multiple sequence alignment, a typical 
   sequence analysis problem in molecular biology, can be solved effectively
   using parallel iterative improvement. In this method, two search
   strategies, best-first and parallel hill-climbing, were used 
   alternatively. Both of them, however, have problems. The best-first 
   search, which rapidly improves state  of solution, is sometimes trapped
   in a locally optimal solution having relatively a low score. The parallel
   hill-climbing method, which distributedly searches for an optimal or
   sub-optimal solution, is frustrating due to its long execution time.
   Multiple sequence alignment can be considered as a combinatorial
   optimaization problem. Its score system, however, is still incomplete,
   so that biologists often compare high-score alignments to extract 
   biological information. Therefore, the multiple alignment method requires
   a new search strategy to rapidly generate sub-optimal alignments. We have
   devised a multi-group parallel search strategy which efficiently solves 
   multiple alignement problems, incorporating the iterative improvement 
   method into the genetic algorithm framework.

3. Progrma Excecution Environment
   This software has two versions;
   one is tha PIM version, that is executable on PIM/m,
   and the other is KLIC version, that is executable on distributed KLIC 
   system.
   We've checked the execution of KLIC version on Sparc Center(20PE).
   
   And we release the performance visulalizing tool "gavtool".
   This program's environment is SUN OS and OpenWare/Motif

4. Papers
   ICOT TR 849:
   Parallel Iterative Aligner with Genetic Algorithm
   Masato Ishikawa, Tomoyuki Toya, Yasushi Totoki, Akihiko Konagaya.

   ICOT TR 855:
   Parallel Iterative Aligner with Genetic Algorithm
   Masato Ishikawa, Tomoyuki Toya, Yasushi Totoki, Akihiko Konagaya.

   Now we are writing a paperin Japanese for Information Processing 
   Society of Japan;
   the tiltle is 
   "Protein Sequence Analysis Using a Multi-Group Parallel Genetic Algorithms"

5. image file
   You can see gavtool window image (gif format) that is the display 
   at execution on PIM/m.
   ALIGNGA/image/crossover0/*.gif : (crossover rate = 0%) execution
   ALIGNGA/image/crossover10/*.gif : (crossover rate = 10%) execution
   
   align??.gif   : alignment display window 
   distrib??.gif : individual distribution window
   info??.gif	 : individual infomation window
   fitness.gif	 : fitness graph window
   (?? = generation number)

6. For install

 gav:
  Both PIM version and KLIC version,
  Please FTP source programs to your machine.
  PIM version is executable on SIMPOS or UNIX(to accecss to PIM/m, use telnet).
  KLIC version is executable on distrbuted KLIC system, 
  please enter "compile" command.

 gavtool:
  Please FTP the files under directory gav as same directory structure.
  In details, please read INSTLALL file.

